        "original_id": "23a8d8a5-238b-537d-ba41-81774715623c",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: The Strongest Man in the World, Roving Mars, Now You See Him, Now You Don't, The Computer Wore Tennis Shoes\n- People: Kurt Russell\n- Organizations: Disney\n- Places: Medfield College, Mars\n- Systems: Mars Exploration Rovers, Spirit, Opportunity\n- Concepts: film sequels, documentary films\n\nFacts:\n- The Computer Wore Tennis Shoes is a 1969 film.\n- The Strongest Man in the World is a 1975 Disney film starring Kurt Russell.\n- In The Strongest Man in the World, Kurt Russell plays a student at the fictional Medfield College.\n- Now You See Him, Now You Don't is a sequel to The Computer Wore Tennis Shoes.\n- The Strongest Man in the World followed Now You See Him, Now You Don't in 1975.\n- Roving Mars is an IMAX documentary film about the development, launch, and operation of the Mars Exploration Rovers.\n- The Mars Exploration Rovers featured in Roving Mars are Spirit and Opportunity.",
